{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394144-which-is-better-transylvania-chronicles-or-ventrue-chronicle","id":1394144,"title":"Which is better, Transylvania Chronicles or Ventrue Chronicle?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-04T13:56:06-07:00","id":1394144,"title":"Which is better, Transylvania Chronicles or Ventrue Chronicle?","content":"I\u2019m probably gonna get to run a short (like five or six sessions) Vampire: the Masquerade game sometime around the end of the year. Which would you recommend, the Transylvania Chronicles or the Ventrue Chronicle? Or maybe the Giovanni Chronicles (though I heard the type in the PDFs is really small and blurry)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T14:01:17-07:00","id":1394146,"title":"","content":"I love the Giovanni and Transylvania Chronicles.<br /> <br /> Never read the Ventrue Chronicles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T14:53:19-07:00","id":1394154,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> thanks \ud83d\ude0a<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a single book chronicle that came out for Revised. I know nothing about it except the name, but my first character was a Roman Ventrue, so I like the clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T14:54:44-07:00","id":1394155,"title":"","content":"Toreador are cool too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T15:25:39-07:00","id":1394165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394144-which-is-better-transylvania-chronicles-or-ventrue-chronicle#post1394144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m probably gonna get to run a short (like five or six sessions) Vampire: the Masquerade game sometime around the end of the year. Which would you recommend, the Transylvania Chronicles or the Ventrue Chronicle? Or maybe the Giovanni Chronicles (though I heard the type in the PDFs is really small and blurry)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Transylvania Chronicles are way, way bigger than 5 or 6 sessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T15:39:16-07:00","id":1394170,"title":"","content":"The first book of Giovanni Chronicles is fun and very straightforward. The text is scanned, but it's readable, and the OCR is good enough that you can search it in your PDF reader. However, it's also <i>really </i>dated mechanically, and the writing is a bit hamfisted (and kind of puerile at times, to be honest). All that said, it's a breezy little adventure you could wrap up in five or six sessions, without the need to necessarily carry on with the rest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T01:00:26-07:00","id":1394277,"title":"","content":"Ventrue though it pales to Nuova Malattia.<br /> <br /> <br /> TC/GC1-3 go from B- to D+.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2782-pittmonkey","name":"Pittmonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2782_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T01:23:45-07:00","id":1394280,"title":"","content":"Thank you guys. Maybe I\u2019ll buy all four Transylvania Chronicles and just run through the first one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T01:28:12-07:00","id":1394281,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2782-pittmonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2782_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2782\" data-vbnamecard=\"2782\">Pittmonkey</a> wow! You post like one post a year. Thanks for responding. I think I might pick up the Ventrue Chronicle too, just because I really like the clan and I\u2019m curious to see what they did with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T05:12:17-07:00","id":1394301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394144-which-is-better-transylvania-chronicles-or-ventrue-chronicle?p=1394281#post1394281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2782-pittmonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2782_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2782\" data-vbnamecard=\"2782\">Pittmonkey</a> wow! You post like one post a year. Thanks for responding. I think I might pick up the Ventrue Chronicle too, just because I really like the clan and I\u2019m curious to see what they did with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hope you enjoy it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T07:04:14-07:00","id":1394326,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1535_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1535\" data-vbnamecard=\"1535\">Jackob</a> thanks \ud83d\ude0a. I think I\u2019m gonna buy Ventrue Chronicle first, before Transylvania Chronicles, so I\u2019ll let you guys know what I think.<br /> <br /> Were you one of the writers? You don\u2019t have to answer if you don\u2019t want to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T10:01:33-07:00","id":1394380,"title":"","content":"I remember it was interesting (Ventrue Chronicles) but I don't think it was a success, because (if I remember correctly) it was supposed to be a saga and they only released one volume...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T13:20:49-07:00","id":1394418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394144-which-is-better-transylvania-chronicles-or-ventrue-chronicle#post1394144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m probably gonna get to run a short (like five or six sessions) Vampire: the Masquerade game sometime around the end of the year. Which would you recommend, the Transylvania Chronicles or the Ventrue Chronicle? Or maybe the Giovanni Chronicles (though I heard the type in the PDFs is really small and blurry)?</div> </div> </div> </div>TC give me a nostalgic feeling. It's an important product, one that shaped metaplot, but in all honesty it's not that good.<br /> Compared to the VC, the TC are much more extensive (4 books vs 1) and the various stories sometimes feel disjointed, simplistic and sometimes fail to give the ST a coherent sequence of events (as it's often the case, the ST needs to fill the gaps).<br /> The VC on the other hand are a self contained much les ambitious project that works well within itself but completely rejects the lofty goals of the TC (a chronicle of ages introducing the end times).<br /> <br /> All in all they are two very different products, if you are willing to work a lot doing the TC can certainly be more rewarding, otherwise go for the VC, which is easier to run and less work intensive for you as the ST.<br /> <br /> P.S.<br /> <br /> The Giovanni Chronicles are similar to the TC in scope and a little better in the execution imo. Be aware that the 4th book (&quot;Nuova Malattia&quot;) implies a radical change compared to the previous three.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 06-05-2020, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T13:44:50-07:00","id":1394424,"title":"","content":"I decided I\u2019m gonna get both \ud83d\ude0a. That way I can read them both and decide which one I like better. Thank you so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T15:55:05-07:00","id":1394443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394144-which-is-better-transylvania-chronicles-or-ventrue-chronicle#post1394144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m probably gonna get to run a short (like five or six sessions) Vampire: the Masquerade game sometime around the end of the year. Which would you recommend, the Transylvania Chronicles or the Ventrue Chronicle? Or maybe the Giovanni Chronicles (though I heard the type in the PDFs is really small and blurry)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Transylvania Transylvania Chronicles starts at the end of XII century and lasts till 1999 (and you could fill the gaps with single adventures like &quot;Under the Black Cross&quot;). There are also rules for downtime (additional XPs for periods between parts of TC) do I think it's too big for 5-6 sessions. On the other hand I think that the story is great because it allows PCs to influence the metaplot.<br /> The same for Giovanni Chronicles: it starts in 1444 and ends at the end of XIX century so it could be too big. Also I find the story less interesting and periods of &quot;inactivity&quot; between parts are greater than in TC. On the other hand the last part (&quot;Nuova Malattia&quot;) requires new characters so I think it could be played during 5 or 6 sessions. Still it's good to read parts 1-3 just to know the story.<br /> Ventrue Chronicles are the worst. It is only one book, composed of 3 stories. In the second one (almost 700 years after the first one) you play a a Child of the character from the first one, in the third, at the end of XX century you play as a Grandchilde of the character from the first one. So it could be played in 5 or 6 sessions but the players won't have time to get into characters. Also the PCs should be Ventrue so your players could not like it.<br /> I'm not a big fan of short games, I prefere the ones which ends by character's death (or player resignation). If I were in your place I would create a big campaign, starting by Ventrue Chronicles (as some kind of Prelude, before the VC beginning), then move to TC (to let PCs gain some XPs and to let players get the atmosphere), then back to the first part of VC, then back to TC and so on. If someone's character dies (and if I don't have any NPC to give to the unfortunate player/s) then I would run first part of GC for them and after that bind the two stories (which could be done during Convention of Thorns in TC part II). BUT it would last waaaayyy too long than your 5-6 sessions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T18:57:31-07:00","id":1394473,"title":"","content":"Ohhhhhhhh<br /> <br /> Okay. Thanks. I\u2019ll probably just get them both and see which one I like better. I\u2019d still like to read Transylvania Chronicles even if I can\u2019t actually run the whole thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T18:59:02-07:00","id":1394474,"title":"","content":"Both chronicles sound pretty good","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T01:41:59-07:00","id":1394524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394144-which-is-better-transylvania-chronicles-or-ventrue-chronicle?p=1394474#post1394474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both chronicles sound pretty good</div> </div> </div> </div>Cause they are. In TC you meet some of the signature V:tM characters (Lucita, Anatole or Myca Vycos) and can shake the future (metaplot). In GC you also meet some of the iconic characters (Durga Syn, Haerstadt) and become a part of the events that leads Giovanni from Bloodline to Clan. Even VC has some good parts, but I still find it the weakest of the three.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 06-06-2020, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T08:13:37-07:00","id":1394564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394144-which-is-better-transylvania-chronicles-or-ventrue-chronicle?p=1394326#post1394326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1535_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1535\" data-vbnamecard=\"1535\">Jackob</a> thanks \ud83d\ude0a. I think I\u2019m gonna buy Ventrue Chronicle first, before Transylvania Chronicles, so I\u2019ll let you guys know what I think.<br /> <br /> Were you one of the writers? You don\u2019t have to answer if you don\u2019t want to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, I did the last chapter. Before having ever actually visited the States. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T08:47:16-07:00","id":1394569,"title":"","content":"Awesome \ud83d\ude00.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T03:20:49-07:00","id":1395565,"title":"","content":"I just read the first part of Ventrue Chronicle.<br /> <br /> Pros: the characters are well-designed and the atmosphere (especially the storm scene) is great.<br /> <br /> Cons: the plot wasn\u2019t super fascinating and one of the key plot points felt kind of forced.<br /> <br /> Overall: I might change a few things for my campaign if I actually end up running this, but I defo didn\u2019t waste my money buying it. Hopefully Part 2 will be even better.<br /> <br /> Also, when we play we tend to play for 10-12 hrs at a shot (we went for 24 hours once after exams), so even though it\u2019s only 5-6 sessions it feels longer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T07:49:10-07:00","id":1396168,"title":"","content":"Part 2 wasn\u2019t as good as part 1. The setting of Gilded Age New York is really cool, but I think except for a couple key characters I\u2019ll probably just get rid of most of the plot and use my own if I end up running the whole Chronicle. Hopefully part 3, set in the aftermath of the Clan Novel story arc from Revised, will be better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T06:24:22-07:00","id":1396663,"title":"","content":"Part 3 was great! All about a Sabbat crusade against Savannah in the late Nineties. I\u2019ll probably use it as written without too many changes.<br /> <br /> Overall Ventrue Chronicle is defo worth the money.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T08:35:29-07:00","id":1396879,"title":"","content":"Late for the answer,<br /> but in my opinion, Transilvanya and Giovanni Chronicles are worth because they are chronicles spanning centuries with roughly the same cast. It's great if you can manage them, but their strength is that you can patch the space between one episode and the next with your own stories.<br /> In that regard, Ventrue Chronicles tries to work in the same frame but ends up being way more free-style.<br /> Arguably, if you miss the first chapter of Transilvanya/Giovanni Chronicles you're in for some troubles later, with Ventrue Chronicle you can plug lore-holes more easily and play only the chronicles you want. While someone may call it a weaker narration, I think is just more flexible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/250518/Dark-Shores-Lineages--of-the-Great-Lakes\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Dark Shores: Lineages of the Great Lakes</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/264262/Fingers-of-the-Eldest-Bogatyri\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Fingers of the Eldest: Bogatyri</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/295115/Forgotten-Alliances\" target=\"_blank\">WTA: Forgotten Alliances</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander","name":"SalamanDer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24483_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T09:25:30-07:00","id":1396890,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24483_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24483\" data-vbnamecard=\"24483\">SalamanDer</a> thank you. I\u2019m gonna read your article on the Bogatyri sometime. I once talked to someone who said he read the Revised Tzimisce Clanbook and he thought the Bogatyri were originally supposed to be Exalted. I\u2019m curious to read your interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T10:04:09-07:00","id":1396897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394144-which-is-better-transylvania-chronicles-or-ventrue-chronicle?p=1396890#post1396890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24483_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24483\" data-vbnamecard=\"24483\">SalamanDer</a> thank you. I\u2019m gonna read your article on the Bogatyri sometime. I once talked to someone who said he read the Revised Tzimisce Clanbook and he thought the Bogatyri were originally supposed to be Exalted. I\u2019m curious to read your interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a book I wrote four-handed with the always excellent Josh Heath and released on the Storyteller's Vault <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> It's a sort of brainstorming we had following the Bogatyri's chapter of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Beckett&#39;s_Jyhad_Diary\" target=\"_blank\">Beckett's Jyhad Diary</a>.<br /> A bit more gory than what I'm used to do, but since it's Tzimisce-stuff it comes with the package.<br /> Plus, we managed to make them sort of playable... and had a lot of fun in the process.<br /> Ok, I'll stop that here because it seems I'm trying to sell you the book :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/250518/Dark-Shores-Lineages--of-the-Great-Lakes\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Dark Shores: Lineages of the Great Lakes</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/264262/Fingers-of-the-Eldest-Bogatyri\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Fingers of the Eldest: Bogatyri</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/295115/Forgotten-Alliances\" target=\"_blank\">WTA: Forgotten Alliances</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander","name":"SalamanDer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24483_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T11:35:21-07:00","id":1396904,"title":"","content":"Okay. Thanks. It\u2019s only $3.99. Maybe I\u2019ll pick it up sometime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T12:57:28-07:00","id":1396923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394144-which-is-better-transylvania-chronicles-or-ventrue-chronicle?p=1396663#post1396663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part 3 was great! All about a Sabbat crusade against Savannah in the late Nineties. I\u2019ll probably use it as written without too many changes.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Happy<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T14:08:18-07:00","id":1396937,"title":"","content":"If you want to run a chronicle of epic proportions, Transylvania Chronicles is your book. Then, if you rather choose something less massive, Ventrue Chronicle introduced a story in which lineage is one of the main theme, it's really great.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T14:10:35-07:00","id":1396939,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1535_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1535\" data-vbnamecard=\"1535\">Jackob</a> and the Prince of Savannah is actually named Penelope \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T14:11:36-07:00","id":1396940,"title":"","content":"@saga I\u2019m gonna buy Transylvania Chronicles I next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T23:46:51-07:00","id":1397012,"title":"","content":"Never read Ventrue Chronicles, but both Giovanni and Transylvanian Chronicles had a suitably epic, multi-century story arc that really drew on the metaplot of the setting in an engaging way. Even if at times they weren't sure WHICH direction they were taking the metaplot. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T01:34:40-07:00","id":1397018,"title":"","content":"Thank you. I\u2019m gonna check out Transylvania Chronicles next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T01:46:20-07:00","id":1397021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1394144-which-is-better-transylvania-chronicles-or-ventrue-chronicle?p=1396939#post1396939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1535_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1535\" data-vbnamecard=\"1535\">Jackob</a> and the Prince of Savannah is actually named Penelope \ud83d\ude0a</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd forgotten that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Lemme hear how the game goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"